WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.860
- Um, Tzuyu, Tsuyu?

00:00:02.793 --> 00:00:04.170
- [Translator] Suyu or chewy.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.280
- Chewy? Okay.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.343
Wait, wait, what?

00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:08.040
- [Translator] Suyu is good.
(audience laughing)

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:08.873
- No, no, Tsuyu?

00:00:08.873 --> 00:00:09.990
How would, how do you say it?

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.910
- [Translator] In Korean, it's chewy.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.960
- Chewy?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.330
How do you want me to say it?

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.040
(Translator speaking in Korean)

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.621
- [Kelly] Chewy?
- Tzuyu.

00:00:18.621 --> 00:00:19.454
- Tzuyu.

00:00:19.454 --> 00:00:21.192
Oh, how you say it's adorable.

00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:24.487
(everyone laughing)

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:27.240
Okay. So, Tzuyu, I think I said it right.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.980
- [Translator] Yeah.
- I'm trying.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.740
So you're performing your single
"MOONLIGHT SUNRISE" today,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.626
so what's the song about?

00:00:33.626 --> 00:00:37.626
(Translator speaking in Korean)

00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:43.797
(Tzuyu speaking in Korean)

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.930
- [Translator] So "MOONLIGHT
SUNRISE" is a song

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.360
about wanting to know
the other person's heart,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.210
and they use the metaphor
of moonlight and sunrise

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.550
to parallel that fluttering heart feeling

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.383
when you're in love.

00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:08.312
- [Kelly] Oh, I like that.
(audience cheers)

